@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="container py-5" style="max-width: 820px;">
    <h1 class="h2 mb-4">Privacy</h1>

    <p class="text-muted">
        This page explains, in plain language, what this system stores about you. The operator of the clinic
        should review it and adapt it to their local legal requirements before going live.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we store</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Your account details: name, address, e-mail address, user name, phone number and an optional profile picture.</li>
        <li>For patients: gender and date of birth.</li>
        <li>Your appointments: the doctor, the date and time, the status and the reason you gave.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Passwords and security</h2>
    <p>
        Passwords are never stored in readable form; only a salted hash is kept. Your e-mail address must be confirmed
        before you can sign in, and too many wrong passwords lock the account for a while.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        The site uses a single sign-in cookie (and an anti-forgery cookie that protects forms). There are no
        advertising or tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who can see your data</h2>
    <p>
        Clinic staff can see appointments and the contact details needed to run the clinic. Patients can only see
        their own appointments.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can update your details at any time from your profile page. To have your account removed, contact the clinic.</p>
</div>
